},{\"desc\":\"Migration inventory labels every remaining provider execution surface managed or legacy_unmanaged, preserves protected provider and cross_host_review timeout ceilings, and documents unsupported platforms plus the same-uid local trust ceiling without claiming cryptographic or authority proof.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:edge:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"An end-to-end real-process smoke submits a run, ends the caller boundary, observes the same run from a new caller with no duplicate spawn, and reaches explicit completed terminal truth whose exact receipt is accepted by the intended formal reviewer consumer.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Operator documentation and diagnostics show how to submit detached work, inspect bounded status, distinguish worker heartbeat from provider progress, cancel, interpret deadline and residual states, decide whether replacement is safe, and recover without restarting on silence.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}}],\"description\":\"Implement the approved ManagedHostRun boundary for CLI-launched cross-provider agents: durable detached/foreground execution, bounded status and cancellation, absolute deadlines, process-group cleanup, honest orphan/replacement safety, ledger-independent shared admission, and exact managed-run receipt binding for formal reviewer evidence. This supersedes heuristic time-window provenance matching such as the inactive B-1be5 proposal; it does not manage native host subagents and must preserve legacy configured provider timeout ceilings.\",\"headHash\":\"8dab841792401ce1e7dcde5f1b1b0a1b28261cb1\",\"materialHash\":\"d23760162146562adba146c0b348370ce78ab2804eb878a2fd8ae263c6a3ffbe\",\"phase\":\"REVIEW\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.full-task-context.v1\",\"scope\":{\"allowedCreate\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md\",\"packa