ipan/work/repo/Prooforstop/.worktrees/B-137a\n\nHost-native task liveness policy:\n- After starting, first output `DISPATCH_START:lattice-review-test-coverage/story` so the host can associate progress with lattice-review-test-coverage/story.\n- Elapsed time or silence alone never proves a stall and never authorizes a replacement.\n- Query the host-native task status for the original task identity.\n- If status is foreground, running, or background, continue bounded polling/waits on that same task identity; do not dispatch a duplicate, including after 10 minutes/600s.\n- If status is unknown or temporarily unavailable, record the uncertainty and keep monitoring the same task identity; do not dispatch a duplicate.\n- If status is completed, consume the original result exactly once.\n- Only an authoritative failed, cancelled, missing, or dead status (or explicit operator cancellation) authorizes at most one replacement.\n- Before replacing, record the terminal reason and ensure the former task can no longer write results or evidence.\n- Explicit configured subprocess deadlines (including provider.codex and cross_host_review) are separate execution contracts and remain enforced.\n\nRole boundary:\n- Review only; do not change code, tests, checklist status, or story metadata.\n- This is a story-level dispatch: review every checklist item and the integrated change, not one selected item.\n\nRequired reading:\n1. .lattice/story/actives/B-137a/background.md\n2. .lattice/story/actives/B-137a/plan.md\n3. .lattice/story/actives/B-137a/checklist.json\n- Read the files and relatedDocs named by every checklist item, bounded by the current candidate-spec artifact.\n- Candidate routing: digest=2e238f39d5e15e10b8ff41c46712df1b8f511ab7cb6ca92e80646014af3ad8ae corpusDigest=3ffd92bd03a28537625b2567c201f6a45109dcacea8d05035d982bbaa3c02b4b candidates=docs/host-run-usage.md, docs/requirements/decisions/proof-admissibility-hardening-execution-plan.md, docs/requirements/decisions/tier-c-cro