attice.managed_review_final_proposal.v1` JSON envelope. The managed adapter seals the strictly validated verdict; the controller cannot supply or override it.\n  Only after state=completed and an exact receiptId exists, call `lattice managed_review_evidence_import '{\"runId\":\"<runId>\",\"receiptId\":\"<receiptId>\"}'`.\n- A raw provider CLI result is manual/advisory output only; it cannot satisfy the managed reviewer evidence path.\n\nConclusion record (must choose one):\n- Native path: start the reviewer run: lattice review_run_start '{\"storyId\":\"B-137a\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-test-coverage\"}' and copy the returned reviewRunId. In the managed cross-provider path the controller already performed this step.\n- Has issues: lattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"B-137a\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId>\",\"desc\":\"<file:line WHY + severity>\",\"severity\":\"high|medium|low\",\"category\":\"missing|edge|adversarial|happy\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-test-coverage\"}'\n- No blocker: call review_pass_set with the returned reviewRunId and a truthful readManifest covering the story-level review.\n\n## Role Prompt\n\n---\nname: lattice-review-test-coverage\ndescription: REVIEW phase reviewer that audits coverage between verificationIntent and verificationEvidence\nmodel: sonnet\ntools: Read, Glob, Grep, Bash\n---\n<!-- proofbound:modular-role-body:v1 -->\nYou are `lattice-review-test-coverage`. Your duty is to inherit the value of the old `TEST_CASE_REVIEW`, but without resurrecting the old phase: you only review during the REVIEW phase whether the `verificationIntent` on the checklist is covered by valid `verificationEvidence`.\n\n## Inputs\n\nThe main agent will give you a storyId. First read:\n\n```bash\nlattice story_get '{\"storyId\":\"<ID>\",\"detail\":true}'\nlattice checklist_get '{\"storyId\":\"<ID>\"}'\nlattice validate '{\"story\":\"<ID>\",\"json\":true}'\n```\n\n## Review Rules\n\n1. For every checklist item, check whether the happy / edge / adversarial intent columns match the current channel:\n   - normal / high-risk / strict: all three columns should exist.\n   - fast / express: at least the happy path should be explainable; missing edge/adversarial may be advisory.\n2. For every intent with priority=`must`, there must be one valid evidence:\n   - `logic_test` / `integration_test` / `browser_test` / `docs_check` / `manual_transcript` whose `result` must not be `fail`.\n   - `waiver` must have a clear note explaining why this story should not be covered by automation.\n3. Evidence must concretely correspond to an intent; broad descriptions such as \"validate passed\" without saying which behavior is covered are not accepted.\n4. If a gap is found, write a finding with `lattice finding_add`:\n\n```bash\nlattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"<ID>\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"category\":\"missing\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-test-coverage\",\"desc\":\"CHK-001:edge:0 lacks valid verificationEvidence; current evidence only covers the happy path\",\"files\":[\"validate.ts\"]}'\n```\n\n## Output\n\nAt the end, output:\n\n- Coverage summary: total intent count, must-gap count, waiver count.\n- List of finding ids that were written.\n- If there are no findings, you must call `lattice review_pass_set '{\"storyId\":\"<ID>\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-test-coverage\",\"note\":\"test coverage review passed: verified coverage between verificationIntent and verificationEvidence, no blocker.\"}'`, then clearly state that the test coverage review passed.\n\nAlways read the canonical reports `acceptance_topology_check`, `pre_review_check_read`, `acceptance_rollout_report_read`, and `acceptance_rollout_check`, and report their status honestly. Missing or non-PASS signed per-Story evidence is a blocker only when a canonical report says `blocking=true`, the project mode is `enforce`, or the work makes an explicit promotion claim. In `observe` or `warn`, `legacy_missing` or `partial` is advisory only: never fabricate a topology and never upgrade it to a formal pass. A report that claims PASS or promotion still requires a current signed receipt and exact full 3 rounds × 2 hosts (`codex-cli` + `claude-cli`); reject degraded 3x1. Prompt prose is never gate evidence. Rollback may only change the configured mode and must preserve every report, receipt, diagnostic, and prior evidence.\n",
.lattice/story/actives/B-137a/review-runs.json:40745:      "assembledPrompt": "## Runtime Contract\n\nLifecycle: INIT -> INIT_CHECK -> PLAN -> DEV -> REVIEW -> TEST -> DONE.\nOnly the Story owner/implementer writes implementation; independent reviewers write signed findings or passes.\nStory and fixture facts use Lattice CLI paths; gate evidence is structured and fail-closed.\nNever fabricate host, human, provider, receipt, or Authority evidence.\n\n## Role Contract\n\n{\"allowedCommandIds\":[\"review_run_start\",\"finding_add\",\"review_pass_set\",\"managed_review_proposal_set\"],\"defaultDispatch\":true,\"forbiddenActionIds\":[\"fabricate-authority\",\"write-outside-role-boundary\"],\"renderDigest\":\"02a7e3ebbe8870564a7bb23a6699e4c4f45e4874c0e3817e5212bd9335beeb95\",\"requiredCheckIds\":[\"scope-and-authority-check\"],\"requiredInputIds\":[\"dispatch-target\",\"project-runtime-guide\"],\"requiredOutputIds\":[\"review-finding-or-pass\"],\"responsibility\":\"Review documentation and code consistency.\",\"roleId\":\"lattice-review-docs\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.role-contract.v1\",\"semanticDigest\":\"54d9bbb24e64e885aea73bd388ce3e7f843b47399822505c1c5c8c216366b4f6\",\"status\":\"active\",\"stopConditionCodes\":[\"missing-required-input\",\"authority-boundary\"]}\n\n## Task Context\n\n{\"checklist\":[{\"context\":\"Introduce the deep ManagedHostRun module with immutable spec/owner/claim, one-shot prompt capability, snapshots/events/live output, absolute deadline, cooperative cancel, exclusive terminal receipt, next-touch reconciliation, replacementSafe, retention and runtimeContinuation semantics. Silence alone never fails or restarts a run.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts\"],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/host-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/runtime-artifact-registry.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/managed-host-run-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-001\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/host-run-usage.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/session-ownership-and-write-leases.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Persist and reconcile managed host-run lifecycle\",\"userSees\":\"用户运行 host_run_status 时看到同一个 runId 的 running/terminal 状态、deadlineAt、workerHeartbeatAt、providerProgress、replacementSafe 和 receiptDigest；静默不会显示为失败或触发新 run。\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Race multiple status, attach, cancel, and reconcile callers at the deadline; exclusive reconciliation and terminal creation must yield one immutable terminal receipt and all callers must converge on its exact digest.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Present missing, corrupt, partially-written, or identity-ambiguous runtime artifacts; the run must fail closed with honest residual unknown and replacementSafe false where cleanup cannot be proven, with no blind kill and no automatic replacement.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Race provider success against cancel and deadline expiry; exactly one authoritative terminal outcome wins, cleanup and residual facts are recorded, and replacementSafe becomes true only when the former execution can no longer write results or evidence.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Keep a real provider fixture silent longer than the legacy first-output and caller-observation boundaries while its process remains alive; repeated next-touch status calls must keep the same run running, report worker liveness separately from provider progress visibility, and never restart it merely because output is absent.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Crash the worker after claim and before terminal publication, then exercise status before and at the finite absolute deadline; reconciliation must preserve the original identity before deadline and eventually materialize definite timed_out or failed terminal truth rather than wait forever.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Submit one managed provider run, observe immutable spec and owner plus a successful worker claim, then observe monotonic snapshots and events ending in exactly one completed terminal receipt whose digest is returned by status; proves the durable lifecycle from submission to terminal truth.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Terminate the original caller after submission while the provider remains active, then query the returned runId from a new caller and observe the same execution continue to completed without a second provider spawn or replacement; proves caller lifetime is not run lifetime.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Make foreground host_run submit-and-attach over the durable run, add detach submission with claim handshake, bounded host_run_status long-poll, idempotent host_run_cancel, and a hidden worker continuation. Keep text/json passthrough contracts and prompt secrecy.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/cli-engine.ts\",\"packages/main/src/cli/command-catalog.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/command-policy.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/host-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/registry.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/managed-host-run-command-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-002\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/host-run-usage.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-codex-command-boundary-execution-plan.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Expose submit, attach, status and cancel command surfaces\",\"userSees\":\"用户用 host_run --detach 得到 runId 后，可用 host_run_status --waitMs 最多等待 30 秒并用 host_run_cancel 幂等取消；前台模式仍显示实时输出，但调用方结束后相同 runId 可继续查询。\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Inspect process arguments, persisted terminal and evidence artifacts, and post-claim runtime files; prompt and capability plaintext must not appear in argv or durable receipts, one-shot inputs must be mode 0600 and removed after claim, and only bounded redacted projections or digests may remain.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Supply unknown, malformed, path-traversal, cross-project, or stale runId values to status and cancel; commands must reject without reading or mutating another run and without spawning any provider process.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Kill the foreground attaching caller while its managed worker is active, then attach from a new caller; the original run must remain observable and complete once, proving CLI watchdog runtimeContinuation cannot translate caller loss into provider cancellation.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Exercise waitMs at 0, 30000, and above 30000 plus a no-change interval; every call is bounded, values above the cap are rejected or capped explicitly, and a wait timeout reports the current non-terminal state without treating it as provider failure.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Call host_run_cancel repeatedly before claim, during execution, and after terminal completion; cancellation is idempotent, targets only the original run, and never creates a second terminal or changes an already authoritative terminal outcome.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Detached host_run returns only after the worker claim handshake with runId, running state, and deadlineAt; host_run_status --waitMs 30000 then long-polls that same identity and returns progress or its terminal receipt, while foreground host_run is submit-and-attach over the identical durable run.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Text and JSON foreground attachment preserve existing routing contracts: text host stdout streams once to stdout, JSON keeps stdout to one result object while transcript streams to stderr, and provider usage and passthrough errors remain honestly represented.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Use POSIX process groups for TERM/KILL/reap/residual checks, fail before spawn on unsupported platforms, launch Codex with documented explicit stdin -, preserve provider usage parsing and configured timeout ceilings, and separate worker heartbeat from provider progress visibility.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/codex-review-leaf.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/host-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/managed-host-run-process-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/provider-codex-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-003\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/host-run-usage.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/tier-c-crosshost-quorum-execution-plan.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Supervise provider processes portably and honestly\",\"userSees\":\"用户看到 silent provider 保持 running 直到真实退出或绝对 deadline；取消/超时结果明确报告 TERM/KILL/reap/residual，Codex 执行使用 stdin '-' 且不会等待未关闭输入。\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Simulate PID or PGID reuse and a mismatched spawn fingerprint at reconcile time; the supervisor must not signal the ambiguous process, must record residual unknown and replacementSafe false, and must not authorize automatic replacement.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Keep the provider silent but alive until its explicit configured absolute deadline; silence alone must not signal or fail it, while the actual deadline must still trigger bounded group cleanup and timed_out terminal truth.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Make stdout and stderr flood, split structured usage records across chunks, and close passthrough sinks asynchronously; supervision must remain bounded, not crash on EPIPE, preserve honest usage availability, and still release process and admission resources.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Exercise a provider leader that exits while a child remains plus a provider that ignores TERM; supervision must check the process group, escalate to KILL after the bounded grace period, reap, and report any residual honestly rather than treating leader exit as full cleanup.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"On an unsupported non-POSIX platform seam, submission must fail before spawn with an explicit unsupported-platform result; no partially supervised child or misleading replacementSafe true may be produced.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"For observable and unobservable providers, snapshots must keep workerHeartbeatAt distinct from lastProviderProgressAt and providerProgressMode; a fresh worker heartbeat cannot be used as evidence of provider output or completion.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:edge:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"On POSIX, launch a fixture that creates a provider process tree in its own group, then complete or cancel it and prove TERM or KILL, reap, and residual probing leave no surviving group member; terminal records the exact cleanup facts.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Launch the Codex adapter through its documented exec stdin sentinel, write the prompt to stdin and close it, then preserve terminal usage parsing and configured provider timeout semantics; proves the managed adapter uses codex exec ... - rather than an undocumented implicit prompt path.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"All provider-process launch sites must acquire the same bounded slot registry even when usage accounting is disabled. Preserve ledger fail-closed behavior, candidate-spec streaming/retention semantics, and explicitly classify remaining migrated/unmanaged execution surfaces.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"packages/main/src/core/provider-process-admission.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/provider-process-registry.ts\"],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/autopilot-executor.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/codex-review-leaf.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/host-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/lattice-dispatch.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/candidate-spec-routing.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/candidate-spec-routing-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/host-run-usage-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/pr

